\[C_{n_{odd}}=\mu_{1}-\mu_{2} \tag{2.1}\] \[C_{n_{even}}=\mu_{1}+\mu_{2}. \tag{2.2}\]

where \(C_{n_{odd}}\) are odd orders cumulants (\(n_{odd}\) represents the orders: 1, 3, 5...), and \(C_{n_{even}}\) are even-order cumulants (\(n_{even}\) represents the orders: 2, 4, 6...). Thus, for a Skellam distribution, the true value of all the odd-order cumulants are identical. The same also holds true for even-order cumulants.

