### 5.2 Systematic uncertainty

While the statistical uncertainties are associated with limited event statistics, the systematic uncertainties are associated with the limitation of the "system." Systematic uncertainties are the uncertainties arising from the protocols followed in the measurement. In this section, we will discuss the systematic uncertainty estimation on cumulant measurements.

